    "stem": "Wafa knows that lines $p$ and $q$ are parallel and that transversal $t$ cuts them. Angle $a$ between $p$ and $t$ measures $140^{\\circ}$. Angle $x$ between $q$ and $t$ is the co-interior angle to angle $a$ on the same side of $t$.\n\nWhich claim about angle $x$ is correct?",
    "item_type": "mcq",
    "options": {
      "A": "Angle $x$ equals $40^{\\circ}$, because co-interior angles on parallel lines sum to $180^{\\circ}$.",
      "B": "Report the words parallel lines as the measure of angle $x$.",
      "C": "Angle $x$ equals $40^{\\circ}$, and that is only the angle next to angle $a$ on the straight line at $p$, with no use of the parallel.",
      "D": "Angle $x$ equals $140^{\\circ}$, the printed measure of angle $a$."
    },
